# Commit format: type(scope): imperative summary
#
# Keep the subject concise: 50 characters preferred, 72 maximum.
# Use the body only when the reason or compatibility impact is not obvious.
#
# Types: feat, fix, refactor, perf, docs, test, chore, build, ci, style, revert
#
# Examples:
#   fix(release): publish tags after build
#   feat(restore): add Telegram archive download
#   docs(readme): clarify restore commands
#
# Body guidance:
# - Explain why the change is needed.
# - Wrap lines at 72 characters.
# - Mention migrations or breaking changes explicitly.
# - Reference issues at the end, for example: Closes #42

type(scope): summary

